{"14":[{"k":"p","t":"Self-Test"},{"k":"p","t":"RAM/ROM Test The RAM/ROM Test screens are shown in Figures 2-4 and 2-2. This test provides a visual check of the game RAM, ROM, and associated circuitry. If the game passes the RAM/ROM Test, the display advances to the Switch Test. The RAM/ROM Test is divided into two sections. The RAM Test is performed first. If the game passes the RAM Test, then after a six-second delay, the self-test goes immediately to the ROM Test without displaying any message. If the game fails the RAM test, a message is displayed in the center of the screen. This message is shown in Table 2-1. The RAM Test continues to run until it passes. If you press and release the red Fire button, the RAM Test advances to the next RAM or ROM Test. If the game passes the ROM Test, no messages are displayed and the self-test advances to the Switch Test. If a ROM fails, a message is displayed. Table 2-2 shows the a message with the location of a failing ROM. If you press and release the red Fire button the ROM Test advances to the next ROM."},{"k":"p","t":"Table 2-1 Faulty RAM Locations"},{"k":"h","t":"Video Location on RAM Type"},{"k":"h","t":"Characteristic Game PCB"},{"k":"tr","t":"Red   6/7L   Upper Video RAM"},{"k":"h","t":"Background 5h Lower Video RAM"},{"k":"tr","t":"Black   16/17C   Upper Video RAM"},{"k":"tr","t":"Background   15/16B   Lower Video RAM"},{"k":"p","t":"Table 2-2 Faulty Program ROM Locations"},{"k":"p","t":"Error Location on"},{"k":"h","t":"Address Game PCB"},{"k":"p","t":"00000 U=6C L=6B 20000 U=4C L=4B Blasteroids"},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 2-1 RAM Test Fails"},{"k":"p","t":"fim, gi OG0000 error"},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 2-2 ROM Test Fails"},{"k":"h","t":"Switch Test"},{"k":"p","t":"Use the Switch Test screen, shown in Figure 2-3, to check the condition of the controls. The Switch Test checks the following buttons: Left Spare Right Spare Left Xform Right Xform Left Thrust Right Thrust Left Fire Right Fire (Left and Right Spares are for factory use.) When you press a button, the name is highlighted on the screen if it is operating properly. Test the operation of the knobs by turning each knob quickly. Eight white numbers should appear below the \u201cted knob\u201d and the \u201cgreen knob\u201d messages on the screen. If any of these numbers are red, the knob mechanism is not working correctly. If any numbers are yellow, the knob is operating poorly. If no num-"}],"15":[{"k":"p","t":"Blasteroids"},{"k":"p","t":"bers appear, the mechanism is unplugged or defective. The number values are for factory use only."},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 2-3 Switch Test"},{"k":"h","t":"Coin Options"},{"k":"p","t":"The Coin Options screen, shown in Figure 2-4, shows the current coin settings. If you want to change these settings, use this screen. To move around the screen, hold down the red Transform button and turn the red knob. If you turn the knob clockwise, you will move down the settings list. If you turn it counterclockwise, you will move up the settings list. You can tell where you are on the screen by looking for the white box around the option. To change a coin option, release the red Transform button and tur the red knob. To cancel all the changes you have made, press the red Thrust button. This restores the settings used before you entered the Self-Test mode. To save all settings and go to the next screen, press the red Fire button. /f you turn off the self-test switch before you press the red Fire button, you will not save the selected coin settings. All of the default settings are shown in green letters. The following are the Blasteroids coin options:"},{"k":"li","t":"* Game Price is the top line on the screen. Turn the red knob to change the game price to one of the four game price settings shown below: One Coin (Default) Three Coins Two Coins Four Coins"},{"k":"li","t":"* Right Mech Multiplier is the second option on the screen. You can choose one of the following multiplier selections: 1 coin counts as 1 coin (Default) 1 coin counts as 4 coins 1 coin counts as 5 coins Self-Test"},{"k":"p","t":"1 coin counts as 6 coins \u00a2 Left Mech Multiplier is the third option on the screen. You can choose one of the following multiplier selections: 1 coin counts as 1 coin (Default) 1 coin counts as 2 coins"},{"k":"li","t":"* Bonus Adder is the last option on the screen. This option has the following settings: No bonus adder (Default) 2 coins give 1 extra coin 4 coins give 1 extra coin 4 coins give 2 extra coin 5 coins give 1 extra coin 3 coins give 1 extra coin Free play (Choose this if you want to use the Demonstration mode.) If you replace the EEROM at location 2A4/B or a hardware problem occurs, all of the coin options will change to the default settings."},{"k":"p","t":"Figure 2-4 Coin Options"},{"k":"p","t":"Table 2-3 Game Option Settings"},{"k":"p","t":"Option Name Available Settings"},{"k":"tr","t":"Restore Factory Options   No   Yes"},{"k":"h","t":"Difficulty Level Easiest Medium Hard"},{"k":"h","t":"Easier Hard"},{"k":"p","t":"Easy Harder Medium Hardest"},{"k":"tr","t":"Clear High   Yes+   No"},{"k":"p","t":"Score Table Demo/Play Mode Playable Game Mode Demonstration Only Mode"},{"k":"tr","t":"Music In Atiract   Yes   No"},{"k":"p","t":"+ Indicates default and manufacturer's recommended settings."}],"36":[{"k":"p","t":"Ulustrated Parts Lists Blasteroids"},{"k":"p","t":"Cabinet-Mounted Assemblies Parts List"},{"k":"p","t":"Part No. Description"},{"k":"p","t":"A043055-01 12-Inch-Long On/Off Harness Assembly"},{"k":"tr","t":"A043713-22   SA Audio PCB Assembly   \u2018"},{"k":"p","t":"A044326-21 Main Blasteroids PCB Assembly A044872-03 Power Supply Assembly"},{"k":"p","t":"A044875-01 AC Power Harness Assembly \u2018A045003-01 Cabinet Assembly A045004-01 Control Panel Assembly A045040-01\u00b0 Communication/Audio (Com/Aud) Harness Assembly"},{"k":"p","t":"A045041-01 Coin Harness Assembly A045042-01 Cabinet Harness Assembly A045044-01 Speaker Harness Assembly A045045-01 Display Har